course: dictionary
lesson: 15036
title: Retail: selling to shoppers
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words tell you how things are sold. Retail is one of them. Look at the words around it: «She works in retail, selling clothes to customers at the big store on the high street.» Working in a store and selling clothes to customers tells you that retail means selling goods to ordinary people.
explain: Ordinary people are called the public. A shop that sells to the public is a retail store. When a shop sells things in small amounts, one item at a time, that is retail. «The shop buys boxes of pens and sells each pen separately.» Buying in boxes and selling single pens is a clue that the shop is doing retail.
explain: Retail can also be a verb, and then it tells you a price. «These trainers retail at $40» means they are sold for $40 in the shops. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "These trainers are sold for $40." If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Retail means selling goods to the public in shops or online, usually in small amounts.
fact: The retail price is the price the shop charges the customer.
fact: A shop buys goods at a wholesale price and sells them at the retail price.
fact: Profit = retail price − wholesale price. If a shop buys a toy for $6 and sells it for $10, its profit is $4.
fact: «Retail therapy» is an informal phrase meaning shopping to cheer yourself up.
exercise: «She works in retail, selling clothes to customers.» What does retail mean? | Making goods in a factory for other businesses | *Selling goods to the public in shops or online | Giving goods away for free | Cleaning the windows of shops
exercise: A shop buys a mug at a wholesale price of $4 and sells it at a retail price of $7. What is its profit? | $7 | *$3 | $11 | $4
exercise: «These shoes retail at $40.» What does retail at mean here? | Cost $40 to repair | *Are sold for $40 in the shops | Were bought by a customer for $40 last year | Are made from $40 worth of leather
test: What does «retail therapy» mean? | *Shopping to cheer yourself up | Selling goods at the wholesale price | Working at a till all day | Paying for a course of medicine
test: A shop's retail price for a jacket is $12 and it paid a wholesale price of $9. What is the profit? | $21 | $12 | *$3 | $9
exam: Which word means selling goods to the public in shops, usually in small amounts? | Profit | *Retail | Customer | Wholesale
